OCMAT 1
# Written by the Aver Engine editor.
# NeonDistrict: "Parametric high-rise building" by randum (@randum), CC BY 4.0 -- https://sketchfab.com/3d-models/parametric-high-rise-building-e6188bfc730b4d1092e34392ca25dc13
NAME NeonDistrict_sf72_window
SHADER standard
BLEND opaque
CULL none
FLAGS twosided=1 castshadow=1 worlduv=0

PARAM baseColorFactor 0.100393 0.140033 0.259705 1
# Not metal: its metal/rough map marks the panes metal 1 / rough 0, a black mirror.
PARAM metallicFactor 0
# Rough 0.12: the source reads as a mirror here (no or a wrong roughness map).
PARAM roughnessFactor 0.12
# Emissive in engine units: 1 = a white wall in full sun, about 33,000 cd/m2. Peak 0.02 = about 670 cd/m2:
# curtain-wall glass (Epsilon_0_0, about 3,000 m2 at x3.6). The source has NO emissive of any kind (five flat spec/gloss colours, no textures), so 'lit balconies' do not exist in this file. The glass is its own material, so a factor lights the whole shell evenly = a fully lit office/hotel tower, broken into ribbons by the black Cover fin grid in front of it. 0.02 = about 670 cd/m2, cool white; it is the only material that should glow..
PARAM emissiveFactor 0.02 0.02 0.02
PARAM normalScale 1
PARAM occlusionStrength 1
PARAM reflectance 0.04
PARAM f90 1
PARAM ior 1.5
PARAM transmission 0
PARAM uvTiling 200
